{"id":"word:hebrew:H2026","type":"word","title":"הָרַג","subtitle":"H2026 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to smite with deadly intent","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to הָרַג (H2026) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 167 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"הָרַג (hârag) means to smite with deadly intent First listed occurrence: 1Chr 7 21."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"הָרַג","transliteration":"hârag","pronunciation":"haw-rag'","strong":"H2026","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2026","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["הָרְג֖וּ","וַ/יַּהֲרֹ֨ג","הָרְג֣וּ","הָרַ֣ג","וַ/יַּהַרְגֵ֖/הוּ"],"morphs":[["HVqp3cp",18],["HC/Vqw3ms",15],["HR/Vqc",13],["HVqp3ms",7],["HVqp2ms",6],["HVqi3ms",6],["HR/Vqc/Sp2ms",4],["HVqp1cs",4],["HC/Vqw3mp",4],["HVqrmsa",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"to smite with deadly intent","usage":"destroy, out of hand, kill, murder(-er), put to (death), make (slaughter), slay(-er), × surely.","full":"H2026. harag הָרַג verb kill, slay (Late Hebrew id. , ואהרג MI (1 singular Imperfect consecutive); Arabic fall into war, conflict, disorder, slaughter ; Sabean הרג fight Os 4, l. 17 , kill SabDenkm 24. 25 ) — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular ׳ה Judg 9:24 4 t., הָרָ֑ג 2Sam 14:7 2 t., וְהָרַג consecutive Isa 27:1 ; suffix וַהֲרָגָ֑נִי consecutive 1Sam 16:2 2 t.; הֲרָגוֺ Gen 4:25 ; etc.; Imperfect יַהֲרֹג Psa 10:8 4 t.; יַהֲרָגֿ Job 5:2 ; וַיַּהֲרֹג Exod 13:15 14 t.; suffix יַהַרְגֵנִי Gen 4:14 ; 1 singular אֶהֱרוֺג Amos 2:3 , אֶהֱרֹג 9:1 ; cohortative וְאַהַרְגָה Gen 27:41 ; suffix וָאֶהֶרְגֵהוּ 2Sam 4:10 ; 2Kin 10:9 ; 3 masculine plural יַהֲרֹ֑גוּ Psa 94:6 ; Ezek 23:47 ; וַיַּהַרְגוּ Gen 34:25 4 t.; suffix יַהַרְגֻנִי 26:7 , etc.; Imperative הֲרֹג Judg 8:20 ; suffix הָרְגֵנִי Num 11:15 ; plural הִרְגוּ 25:5 2 t.; הֲרֹ֑גוּ 31:17 ; Infinitive absolute הָרֹג 11:15 2 t.; הָרוֺג Est 9:16 ; construct הֲרֹג Exod 2:15 11 t.; הֲרוֺג Eccl 3:8 ; Est 7:4 ; suffix הָרְגֵנִי Exod 2:14 ; הָרְגֵנוּ 5:21 ; הֲרָגְךָ 1Sam 24:11 ; הָרְגֶ֑ךָ Gen 27:42 2 t.; הָרְגוֺ Exod 21:14 ; Participle active הֹרֵג Gen 4:15 4 t.; הוֺרֵג Ezek 21:16 ; הֹרְגֶ֑ךָ 28:9 ; הֹרְגִים Jer 4:31 ; 2Kin 17:25 ; passive הֲרוּגִים Isa 10:4 2 t.; הֲרֻגִים 14:19 ; construct הֲרֻגֵי Jer 18:21 ; הֲרוּגָיו Isa 27:7 ; הֲרוּגֶיהָ 26:21 ; הֲרֻגֶיהָ Prov 7:26 ; &#8212; 1. a. kill, slay , implying ruthless violence, especially private violence Gen 4:8 , 14 , 15 , 23 , 25 ; 12:12 (all J), 20:11 (E) 26:7 ; 27:41-42 , 34:25-26 , 37:20 , 26 (all J), 49:6 (poem in J), Exod 2:14 (twice in verse); 2:15 (E), 5:21 (J) 21:14 ; 23:7 (both J E), Num 31:19 (P) Judg 9:5 , 18 , 24 (twice in verse); 9:56 ; 16:2 ; 20:5 ; 1Sam 16:2 ; 22:21 ; 24:11 ; 24:12 ; 24:18 ; 2Sam 3:30 ; 4:10-11 , 12 ; 12:9 ; 14:7 ; 23:21 ; 1Kin 2:5 , 32 ; 18:12-13 , 14 ; 19:1 , 10 , 14 ; 2Kin 9:31 ; 10:9 ; 1Chr 7:21 ; 11:23 ; 2Chr 21:4 , 13 ; 22:8 ; 24:23 , 25 ; 25:3 ; Neh 4:5 ; 6:10 (twice in verse); Zech 11:5 ; Psa 10:8 ; 94:6 (|| רִצֵּחַ ); compare Judg 8:18-19 , 20 , 21 ; 9:54 ; 1Kin 12:27 ; Isa 14:20 ; 2Chr 22:1 ; Neh 9:26 ; so of massacre of Jews planned by Haman Est 3:13 ; 7:4 (both וּלְאַבֵּד לַהֲרֹג לְהַשְׁמִיד ), and of slaughter of Jews' enemies in defence and revenge 8:11 (same combination) 9:6 , 10 , 12 , 15 , 16 compare 9:11 (passive participle the slain ). b. hence of wholesale slaughter after battle Num 31:7-8 , (twice in verse); 31:17 (twice in verse) (all P), Josh 8:24 ; 10:11 (both J E), 13:22 (P), Judg 7:25 (twice in verse); 8:17 ; 9:45 ; 2Sam 10:18 ; 1Kin 9:16 ; 11:24 ; 2Kin 8:12 ; 1Chr 19:18 ; 2Chr 28:6-7 , 9 ; 36:17 ; Ezek 26:8 , 11 , compare Judg 9:26 ; passive participle the slain Isa 10:4 ; 14:19 compare Ezek 23:10 , 47 ; 37:9 ; Jer 18:21 מָוֶת הֲרֻגֵי (|| מֻכֵּיחֶֿרֶב ); further Hosea 9:13 ; Hab 1:17 ; Jer 4:31 ; Ezek 21:16 ; 28:9 ; also of slaughter in a revolt 2Kin 11:8 2Chr 23:17 . 2 of God's slaying in judgment (stern and inscrutable), Gen 20:4 (E), Exod 4:23 ; 13:15 ; 22:23 (all J E), Amos 2:3 ; 4:10 ; 9:1 , 4 ; Lam 2:4 , 21 ; 3:43 ; Psa 59:12 ; 78:31 ; 78:34 ; 135:10 ; 136:18 compare Num 11:15 (twice in verse) (JE), 22:33 (J), Isa 14:30 , 26:21 (passive the slain , so 27:7 ), Jer 15:3 ; figurative בְּאִמְרֵיפִֿ֑י הֲרַגְתִּים Hosea 6:5 (|| חָצַבְתִּי בַּנְּבִיאִים ). 3 rarely of judicial killing by men (at God's command), Exod 32:27 (JE), Lev 20:15-16 , (H), Num 25:5 (JE), Deut 13:10 (twice in verse) compare Ezek 9:6 לְמַשְׁחִית תַּהַרְגוּ . 4 of killing beasts , Num 22:29 (J; Balaam's ass), Lev 20:15 compare above, Isa 22:13 (oxen; || שָׁחֹט ), בַּיָּ֑ם אֲשֶׁר הִתַּנִּין 27:1 ; also of killing vines, by hail Psa 78:47 . 5 of killing by beasts: lions 2Kin 17:25 , viper Job 20:16 . 6 quite General is לִרְמּוֺא וְעֵת לַהֲרוֺג עֵת Eccl 3:3 . 7 destroy, ruin קִנְאָה תָּמִית וּפֹתֶה יַהֲרָגכָּֿ֑עַשׂ לֶאֱוִיל Job 5:2 ; תְּאַבְּדֵם סִילִים כְּ וְשַׁלְוַת תַּהַרְגֵם מְּתָיִם מְשׁוּבַת Prov 1:32 ; also of those ruined by shameless woman 7:26 . &#8212; Regular construction is with accusative; object sometimes omitted, as Lam 2:21 ; used absolute Hosea 9:13 ; Jer 4:31 ; 15:3 ; Lam 3:43 ; Ezek 21:16 ; Eccl 3:3 ; followed by בְּ slay among , i.e. some of, 2Kin 17:25 ; 2Chr 28:6 , 9 ; Psa 78:31 ; followed by מִן (part of), + accusative, 1Chr 19:18 ; followed by direct object with לְ 2Sam 3:30 ; Job 5:2 ; Psa 135:11 = 136:19 ; 136:20 (but in last 3 first object is accusative). Niph`al Imperfect 1 passive of Qal 1 a , יֵהָרֵג Lam 2:20 shall priest and prophet be slain in the sanctuary? 2 passive of Qal 1 b , 3 feminine plural תֵּהָרַגְנָה Ezek 26:6 ; also 26:15 הֶרֶג בֵּהָרֵג ( = בְּהֵהָרֵג ), but ᵐ5 Co חֶרֶב בַּהֲרֹג . Pu`al Perfect 3masculine singular הֹרָ֑ג Isa 27:7 be slain (passive of Qal 1 b ); compare 1 plural הֹרַגְנוּ Psa 44:23 (|| טִבְחָה כְּצאֹן נֶחְשַׁבְּנוּ ).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 7 21","keyReferences":["1Chr 7 21",